{"id": "city-option-inactive-worker-health-funds", "title": "Unclaimed worker health funds moved into San Francisco’s General Fund", "seconds": 79.9, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "c9accea0cc2c387d", "words": 250, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "San Francisco transferred 201 million dollars from inactive worker health accounts to its General Fund.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.8, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["Where", "did", "the", "health", "benefits", "go?"], "sub": "SF City Option"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.81, 1.31, 1.61, 1.94, 2.13, 2.42, 2.76, 2.98, 3.44, 3.74, 3.94, 4.59, 4.75, 4.89, 5.2]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "Public Health reported about 138,000 accounts in the first closure cycle.", "t0": 5.92, "t1": 10.0, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "results", "kicker": "San Francisco Department of Public Health", "text": "May 2026", "mark": "May 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.54, 0.93, 1.18, 1.35, 1.62, 2.04, 2.37, 2.78, 2.88, 2.99, 3.24, 3.58]}, {"scene": "historic", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Years earlier, auditors had traced separate transfers of 17.5 million dollars to Public Health.", "t0": 10.22, "t1": 14.97, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "audit", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller’s Office, independent audit by Sjoberg Evashenk Consulting", "text": "2020 audit", "mark": "2020 audit"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.74, 1.18, 1.27, 1.55, 1.9, 2.4, 2.51, 2.94, 3.18, 3.43, 3.69, 3.99, 4.1, 4.39]}, {"scene": "historic", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "The audit found the transfers complied with the contract. The department did not track its spending.", "t0": 15.09, "t1": 19.68, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Transfers under the contract"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.39, 0.57, 0.67, 1.13, 1.48, 1.61, 1.71, 2.69, 2.86, 3.37, 3.55, 3.72, 4.0, 4.12]}, {"scene": "historic", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "The audit also found 359 million dollars awaiting enrollment or assignment to a program.", "t0": 19.8, "t1": 25.07, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "audit", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller’s Office, independent audit by Sjoberg Evashenk Consulting", "text": "February 2020", "mark": "February 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.53, 0.87, 1.1, 1.34, 1.64, 2.22, 2.57, 3.01, 3.42, 3.94, 4.06, 4.56, 4.7, 4.77]}, {"scene": "historic", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Under the earlier policy, workers could reopen their accounts and restore their balances.", "t0": 25.19, "t1": 29.59, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Deactivated accounts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.4, 0.76, 1.62, 2.05, 2.22, 2.57, 2.71, 3.13, 3.27, 3.57, 3.72]}, {"scene": "policy", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "A second audit found Public Health complied with the ordinance, but lacked outcome measures.", "t0": 29.81, "t1": 34.09, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "companion", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller’s Office, independent audit by Sjoberg Evashenk Consulting", "text": "2022 oversight audit", "mark": "2022 oversight audit"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.46, 0.76, 0.99, 1.32, 1.57, 1.96, 2.08, 2.19, 2.92, 3.12, 3.38, 3.76]}, {"scene": "policy", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "In October 2022, 830 million dollars moved into City treasury custody. The funds still belonged to workers.", "t0": 34.21, "t1": 40.77, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$830 million", "label": "October 2022 treasury transfer"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.55, 0.79, 1.48, 1.71, 2.0, 2.25, 2.51, 3.03, 3.3, 3.47, 3.71, 4.07, 5.04, 5.2, 5.42, 5.63, 5.91, 6.0]}, {"scene": "policy", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "The Health Commission approved permanent closure after three years of inactivity and notice.", "t0": 40.89, "t1": 45.01, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "resolution", "kicker": "San Francisco Health Commission", "text": "March 2023 policy", "mark": "March 2023 policy"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.34, 0.71, 1.12, 1.55, 1.99, 2.27, 2.55, 2.79, 2.9, 3.5, 3.62]}, {"scene": "policy", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "The commission recommended using the reclaimed funds for health care.", "t0": 45.13, "t1": 48.25, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Health care services"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.6, 1.17, 1.45, 1.59, 2.08, 2.43, 2.58, 2.81]}, {"scene": "policy", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "The initial snapshot was 507 million dollars. Many accounts did not end up in the transfer.", "t0": 48.37, "t1": 53.4, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "First closure cycle", "heading": "Snapshot and actual transfer", "source": "results", "rows": [{"icon": "calendar", "label": "March 2023 snapshot", "value": "$507 million"}, {"icon": "transfer", "label": "May 2026 transfer", "value": "$201 million"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.44, 0.97, 1.13, 1.42, 1.71, 1.98, 2.26, 3.12, 3.36, 3.69, 3.84, 4.02, 4.19, 4.32, 4.41, 4.5]}, {"scene": "policy", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "Across four years the program paid 634.4 million dollars in claims, including older balances.", "t0": 53.52, "t1": 60.04, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "results", "kicker": "San Francisco Department of Public Health", "text": "Four years of claims", "mark": "Four years of claims"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.63, 0.94, 1.05, 1.44, 1.68, 1.95, 2.24, 2.94, 3.24, 3.57, 3.93, 4.27, 4.38, 5.13, 5.6, 5.86]}, {"scene": "reserve", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "The Controller’s reserve plan used a 220.8 million dollar estimate for the transfer.", "t0": 60.26, "t1": 65.47, "shot": "r12", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "budget", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller’s Office", "text": "June 2026 budget estimate", "mark": "June 2026 budget estimate"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.65, 1.01, 1.39, 1.61, 1.69, 1.9, 2.18, 2.56, 2.87, 3.19, 3.58, 3.89, 4.33, 4.46, 4.57]}, {"scene": "reserve", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "The public budget identifies a reserve without tracing each dollar of spending.", "t0": 65.59, "t1": 68.79, "shot": "r13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "General Fund reserve"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.38, 0.7, 1.21, 1.29, 1.64, 1.9, 2.25, 2.43, 2.67, 2.75]}, {"scene": "reserve", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "Officials also described a grievance process for workers who dispute a closure.", "t0": 68.91, "t1": 72.56, "shot": "r14", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "minutes", "kicker": "San Francisco Health Commission", "text": "Grievance review", "mark": "Grievance review"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.54, 0.85, 1.22, 1.29, 1.69, 2.16, 2.31, 2.66, 2.78, 3.1, 3.16]}, {"scene": "reserve", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "next[0]"], "text": "The records leave open individual closure outcomes and the final use of the transferred money.", "t0": 72.68, "t1": 76.77, "shot": "r15", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Contested closures", "Final expenditures"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.49, 0.71, 1.01, 1.52, 1.89, 2.39, 2.55, 2.67, 2.98, 3.17, 3.25, 3.34, 3.79]}, {"scene": "reserve", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 76.89, "t1": 79.03, "shot": "r16", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.65, 0.8, 1.06, 1.17, 1.26, 1.5, 1.76]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Money from inactive accounts", "historic": "The earlier transfers", "policy": "A different policy", "reserve": "Where the money went"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "number"}